core_based_statistical_area.description:
Geographical area maintained by US Office of Management and Budget (OMB) which consists of one or more counties anchored by an urban center.
CBSAs are categorized as Metropolitan (at least one urbanized area of 50,000+ inhabitants) or Micropolitan (at least one urban cluster of between 10,000 and 50,000 inhabitants);
these are also referred to as MSAs (5 digits).
